                        <cell rendition="#border-bottom" rows="22">
                            <p>The undersigned having sold to the Confederate States of America, and
                                received the value of same in bonds, the receipt whereof is hereby
                                acknowledged, 57 bales of cotton, marked, numbered, and classed as
                                in the margin, which are now deposited at his plantation in said
                                county, hereby agrees to take due care of said cotton while on his
                                plantation, and to deliver the same, at his own expense, at Canton,
                                on the N. O., I. &amp; G. N. railroad, in the State of Mississippi,
                                to the order of the secretary of the treasury, or his agents, or
                                their assigns.</p>
                            <p rendition="#right">THOS. G. SMITH.</p></cell>
